We can use this proportion:

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle ABC
\\
{\text{opposite to } \atop 55\degree\text{ angle}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\maroonD{\dfrac{BC}{8.2}}=\blueE{\dfrac{AB}{10}}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&\scriptsize\text{hypotenuse}
\\
&\text{triangle }\boxed{2}
\end{array}$



[[☃ image 1]]

Now we can rewrite the equation to show the ratios of the side lengths *within* each triangle.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&{\text{opposite to } \atop 55\degree\text{ angle}}
\\
\scriptsize\triangle ABC
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{BC}{AB}=\dfrac{8.2}{10}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&\scriptsize\text{triangle }\boxed{2}
\\
&\scriptsize\text{hypotenuse}
\end{array}$
